<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Wide Streets Commission</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1757">1757</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Wide Streets Commission was a body set up by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/parliament-of-ireland">Irish Parliament</a> in 1757 to lay out a broad new street from Essex Bridge to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dublin-castle">Dublin Castle</a>. Over the following decades it planned much of Georgian <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dublin">Dublin</a>, including Parliament Street, Westmoreland Street and D'Olier Street and the widening of Sackville Street, now O'Connell Street.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/wide-streets-commission.jpg" alt="Wide Streets Commission" width="320" height="216" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Oliver Grace · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Sackville_St_and_Gardiner%27s_Mall_in_the_1750s_by_Oliver_Grace.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
